{geni:about_me} Nerissa J. Fuller, a homemaker and former nursing assistant, died Jan. 29 from complications of diabetes at the home of her son in San Jose, Calif. She was 69.

The former Baltimorean, who moved to San Jose in 1977, was born Nerissa J. Dixon. She was a 1947 graduate of Douglass High School and the Johns Hopkins School of Nursing.

She was married to Richard Fuller, who died in 1983.

A memorial service was Feb. 3 in California.

She is survived by three sons, Wayne Epps of Baltimore, Marvin Epps of San Jose and Andre Savoy of Sacramento, Calif.; two daugh',NULL,NULL),
